<item><title>MPEC seeks to unseat ruling party in Dja and Lobo’s five seats</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/mpec-seeks-to-unseat-ruling-party-in-dja-and-lobo-s-five-8e36f8/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/mpec-seeks-to-unseat-ruling-party-in-dja-and-lobo-s-five-8e36f8/</guid><category>Cameroon</category><description>Professor Jean-Calvin Aba’a Oyono leads a six-person slate challenging the ruling party’s hold on the department’s National Assembly seats.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 08:27:11 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" length="34085" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Cameroon opens study for first national electricity tariff policy</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-opens-study-for-first-national-electricity-tariff-819b4c/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-opens-study-for-first-national-electricity-tariff-819b4c/</guid><category>Cameroon</category><description>Consultations began in Yaoundé on November 25 to examine pricing principles, social tariffs, targeted subsidies and equalization.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:33:25 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" length="34085" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
