<item><title>Cameroon lifts domestic share of public investment funding to 62.6%</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-lifts-domestic-share-of-public-investment-funding-52d8f3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-lifts-domestic-share-of-public-investment-funding-52d8f3/</guid><category>Cameroon</category><description>Finance Minister Louis Paul Motaze said domestic funding rose by CFA261 billion in 2025, while external funding fell by CFA13.9 billion.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:40:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-lifts-domestic-share-of-public-investment-funding-52d8f3/share.jpg" length="44022" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-lifts-domestic-share-of-public-investment-funding-52d8f3/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
